                     /note="repA101ts: the pSC101 replication initiation protein
                     as carried by the curable Red helper plasmid pKD46 — the
                     canonical rep allele with H289Y. Sequence of record:
                     AY048746 (pKD46, Datsenko & Wanner 2000) CDS
                     complement(3496..4446), protein AAL02049.1. It differs from
                     the catalog's rep pSC101 (the native pSC101 allele of
                     NC_002056) at exactly one residue, H289Y, and from UniProt
                     P22308 at H257R. This is the allele of the pSC101 replicons
                     that are grown at 30 degrees and cured at 37; which residue
                     causes that temperature sensitivity is NOT established
                     here. Armstrong et al. 1984 located pSC101's
                     temperature-sensitive, copy-number and
                     replication-deficient mutations inside rep101 rather than
                     in the origin, but give no residue, and the GenBank record
                     names this CDS repA101 without stating a phenotype. No
                     origin part in this catalog carries a
                     temperature-sensitivity claim."
